{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"strict-downset-maximal","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Maximality of the strict downset among proper sieves"}]},"title_text":"Maximality of the strict downset among proper sieves","kind":"theorem","taxon":null,"url":"strict-downset-maximal.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","strict-downset-maximal"],["kind","theorem"],["label","Theorem"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Call a "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"direct-category","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"direct structure"}]}},{"Text":" "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"reflecting"}]},{"Text":" when every morphism between objects of equal degree is a split epimorphism. In a reflecting direct category, every non-invertible-in-degree morphism strictly raises degree, and the "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"strict-downset-sieve","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"strict downset"}]}},{"Text":" is as large as a proper sieve can be:"}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"If the direct structure is reflecting, then every "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"proper-maximal-sieve","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"proper sieve"}]}},{"Text":" "},{"Math":{"src":"S"}},{"Text":" on "},{"Math":{"src":"x"}},{"Text":" refines into the strict downset:"}]},{"Math":{"src":"S ⊆ sans(\"StrictDown\") lr(( x )) ."}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"For suppose "},{"Math":{"src":"S ∋ f"}},{"Text":" with "},{"Math":{"src":"f : y -> x"}},{"Text":" of equal degree. By reflection "},{"Math":{"src":"f"}},{"Text":" has a section "},{"Math":{"src":"s"}},{"Text":", and closure under precomposition gives "},{"Math":{"src":"S ∋ s ⋆ f = sans(\"id\")_x"}},{"Text":", contradicting properness. So every member of "},{"Math":{"src":"S"}},{"Text":" strictly raises degree, which is membership in "},{"Math":{"src":"sans(\"StrictDown\") lr(( x ))"}},{"Text":"."}]}]}}}]}}
